WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:01.901
-Hey, everybody.

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:04.837
Welcome to another
"Tonight Show: At Home Edition."

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:06.071
My name is Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:06.071 --> 00:00:08.441
And, man, we've made it through
another week.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.977
I want to say
this is 40-something days?

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.379
[ Chuckles ] That's --
That's how I can tell, yeah.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:15.214
It's 40-something.

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:17.183
A lot of people are starting
to crack a little bit,

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.617
maybe stressing out
a little bit,

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:21.420
but I'm -- I'm hitting my point
a little bit.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:24.957
I'm going a little crazy,
but I think

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:26.826
let's not be
the exception to the rule.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:29.862
I think we are Americans,
but I think, as Americans,

00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:33.232
let's let people --
let's get out of the way

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:36.236
for people that need to
do stuff, they can do stuff.

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:38.771
And soon, I'm promising you,

00:00:38.771 --> 00:00:40.272
we're gonna
get through this together.

00:00:40.272 --> 00:00:43.642
And when we come back, we'll be
stronger and better than ever.

00:00:43.642 --> 00:00:46.478
But this is a time where we just
got to get each other's back

00:00:46.478 --> 00:00:49.215
and know that we're all
going through this together.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.483
So, thank you again
for watching,

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:53.053
and I want to thank my daughter
for drawing this

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:55.988
and kind of misspelling
my own name now.

00:00:55.988 --> 00:00:58.057
I just -- at this point,
everybody's distracted.

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:00.325
I get it.

00:01:00.325 --> 00:01:02.462
Let's make some jokes.

00:01:04.263 --> 00:01:05.865
Guys, it's Friday, which means

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:08.367
it's time to celebrate
the end of another long week

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:10.136
with a Lysoltini!

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.005
Ow-ooh!

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:14.273
Who knows? Maybe I'll have
a "sex on the bleach."

00:01:14.273 --> 00:01:18.444
I don't know. Let's just see
where the night takes me.

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:19.812
During his press conference
last night,

00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:21.314
President Trump suggested that

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:25.351
the virus could be killed
by injecting disinfectants.

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.019
Even the mayor of Las Vegas
was like,

00:01:27.019 --> 00:01:29.455
"That sounds dangerous."

00:01:29.455 --> 00:01:31.057
Trump also suggested using heat

00:01:31.057 --> 00:01:32.859
or a very powerful light
on the body

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.227
to kill the virus.

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:35.461
Trump was like,
"That's why I stared

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:37.230
directly into the eclipse."

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.033
But, today, Trump said that

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:44.937
his comments on ingesting
disinfectants were sarcastic.

00:01:44.937 --> 00:01:46.605
When he heard that,
Chandler Bing was like,

00:01:46.605 --> 00:01:48.842
"Could you be
any more out of it?"

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:54.214
Guys, last night was the start
of the NFL Draft,

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:57.183
and general managers tried to
re-create their offices at home,

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:58.584
but not everyone
had the same setup.

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:01.687
For instance,
here's the 49ers' GM's setup.

00:02:01.687 --> 00:02:03.857
And here's
Bill Belichick's setup.

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:07.059
He looks like a dad comparing
flights for a trip to Reno.

00:02:07.059 --> 00:02:08.994
[ Laughs ]

00:02:08.994 --> 00:02:10.463
He looks like a dad
trying to figure out

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:14.533
how to get photos from his
old laptop onto his new laptop.

00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:15.968
Hey, Churchill Downs
announced that

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.537
it will air a virtual,
computer-simulated version

00:02:18.537 --> 00:02:20.607
of the Kentucky Derby.

00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:22.408
Not only is the Derby
going virtual,

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.577
but it seems like the virus
has even affected

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.212
which horses are racing.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:30.249
For example,
there's Reluctant Zoomer.

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:32.985
Then there's SweatPrance.

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:36.155
There's also Join with Audio.

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:39.024
Then there's Masked Millie.

00:02:39.024 --> 00:02:43.696
And, of course, See It
(ButDon'tTouch) It Biscuit.

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:46.198
Good luck to all of those
virtual horses.

00:02:46.198 --> 00:02:47.400
Check this out --

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.668
Pillsbury announces
that their cookie dough

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:51.837
will soon to be safe to eat
either baked or raw.

00:02:51.837 --> 00:02:53.506
Americans heard that
and were like,

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.241
"What do you mean by 'soon'?"

00:02:58.344 --> 00:03:00.279
A little space work.

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:01.981
That's cookie dough space work.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:03.315
Hey, here's some good news --

00:03:03.315 --> 00:03:06.418
actor Richard Gere is
the father of a new baby boy.

00:03:06.418 --> 00:03:08.354
Yeah. He's 70 years old,

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:09.722
which is why the boy's
first words

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:13.025
will either be "Mama"
or "Grandpa."

00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:16.429
A new survey found that only
18% of couples in quarantine

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:19.031
are satisfied with communication
with their partner.

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:23.836
The remaining 82% didn't really
want to talk about it.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.605
And, finally,
scientists say that,

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:26.939
next week, a giant asteroid

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:29.808
is expected to just miss
colliding with Earth.

00:03:29.808 --> 00:03:31.510
People on Earth heard that
and were like,

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.713
"I'll take anything to get me
out of this Zoom meeting."

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:35.281
Ha ha!
There you go.

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.649
That's our monologue,
everybody.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:37.917
We have a great show tonight.

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.685
Oh, my gosh.
These guys are on fire.

00:03:39.685 --> 00:03:42.388
I love them so much.
The Jonas Brothers are on.

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:44.757
They secretly dropped this thing
last night at midnight

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:46.292
called "Happiness Continues."

00:03:46.292 --> 00:03:47.893
It's on Amazon Prime Video.

00:03:47.893 --> 00:03:51.530
We'll be talking to the three --
the three kids and figure out --

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:52.798
I guess they're not
even kids anymore.

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:54.900
Gosh, they have families now.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.402
But we will be talking
to the Jonas Brothers.

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.703
I love those guys --

00:03:57.703 --> 00:03:59.471
always working hard
and doing something different.

00:03:59.471 --> 00:04:01.374
We'll talk about the new album,
and we're going to play a game

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:07.513
of quarantine admissions --
let's just say that.

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:09.082
[Chuckling] Things --
Things we've done in quarantine

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:10.449
that we're afraid to admit.

00:04:10.449 --> 00:04:12.718
Also on the show, we have

00:04:12.718 --> 00:04:15.355
host of "NBC Nightly News"
and NBC "Dateline" --

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:17.723
he also has a
"Nightly News: Kids Edition"

00:04:17.723 --> 00:04:19.591
that you should check out
on YouTube.

00:04:19.591 --> 00:04:22.228
Lester Holt is on the show
tonight.

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:24.229
We love having Lester
on the show.

00:04:24.229 --> 00:04:26.965
And musical guests -- from
our Scottish friends CHVRCHES.

00:04:26.965 --> 00:04:28.534
We love CHVRCHES so much!

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.470
♪♪

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.604
-Wepa!

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:33.605
-Hey, guys, it's Friday.
[ Applauds ]

00:04:33.605 --> 00:04:35.040
That's right -- it's Friday,
and that's usually

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:38.144
when I send out my "thank you"
notes to everybody.

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:40.679
-I know it's Friday!
-So -- You did?

00:04:40.679 --> 00:04:42.147
How did you know it was Friday?

00:04:42.147 --> 00:04:46.084
-Because -- Because, um,
I don't have -- You know what?

00:04:46.084 --> 00:04:49.522
Only on Fridays and Saturdays,
I don't have --

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:51.858
I don't need to do Raz-Kids.

00:04:51.858 --> 00:04:53.459
-Oh, the reading?
-Yeah.

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:54.793
-Okay, yeah.
Only on Fridays and Saturdays.

00:04:54.793 --> 00:04:55.995
But every -- the rest
of the week, you're always --

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:57.029
-Yeah.

00:04:57.029 --> 00:04:58.030
-That's how you know
it's Friday.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.565
-Uh-huh.
-Yep.

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:01.067
Well, how about --

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:03.736
Also, we send out "thank you"
notes on Fridays, don't we?

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:05.004
-Yeah.
-No.

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:06.839
-What did you say, Fran?
-"No."

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:08.775
-Okay.

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:11.077
So, we do send out
"thank you" notes.

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:12.745
Do you want me to do your job?

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:16.015
-No, I want to do my job.
-Okay, thank you.

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:17.416
Alright, can I get

00:05:17.416 --> 00:05:19.184
some "thank you" note writing
music, please, Frannie?

00:05:19.184 --> 00:05:20.653
[ Music plays ]
-Daddy.

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:25.224
♪♪

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:27.260
-That's just -- There you go.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.428
Thank you so much.

00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:33.599
Thank you, Bill de Blasio --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:36.201
Winnie, do you want
to press the screen?

00:05:36.201 --> 00:05:37.970
-I'm busy coloring.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.305
-[ Chuckles ]

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:40.506
-Okay.

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:43.976
♪♪

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:45.845
Yeah, I know, Frannie.
Guess what --

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:49.048
I took the boos off of
that thing so you can't boo me.

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:52.951
[ Laughs ]
Yee! Daddy wins again!

00:05:52.951 --> 00:05:54.019
-No.

00:05:54.019 --> 00:05:55.687
♪♪

00:05:55.687 --> 00:05:58.291
-Thank you --
-[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:05:58.291 --> 00:06:01.060
Pbht! [ Laughs ]

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:03.896
-You could make
your own sound effects, I guess.

00:06:03.896 --> 00:06:05.898
Yeah.
Alright, let's go. Ready?

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:07.266
Give me some music.

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:09.068
Can you sit up, please, guys?

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:10.870
-Boo!

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:12.671
[ Laughs ]
I made it.

00:06:12.671 --> 00:06:14.173
Boo!

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:15.441
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:16.375
-Oh.

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:17.709
-Boo!
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.709 --> 00:06:21.914
-How'd you -- How'd you learn
how to do that button?

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:23.482
-Boo!

00:06:23.482 --> 00:06:25.284
-How did she learn to do that?
-I do not know.

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:27.753
-Alright, can you give me some
piano music, please, please?

00:06:27.753 --> 00:06:31.190
-Boo! Boo!
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:32.591
-Thank you...
-Boo!

00:06:32.591 --> 00:06:34.293
-...Bill de Blasio,
for announcing that

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:37.329
New York's 4th of July
fireworks show will go on --

00:06:37.329 --> 00:06:41.234
or, as dogs put it, "2020
literally could not get worse."

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:42.668
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.668 --> 00:06:45.971
-Boo!
[ Laughter ]

00:06:45.971 --> 00:06:48.807
-Thank you, Insane Clown Posse,

00:06:48.807 --> 00:06:50.942
for canceling this year's
Gathering of the Juggalos

00:06:50.942 --> 00:06:54.914
and showing that you're actually
a Rational Clown Posse.

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:56.516
-[ Chuckles ]

00:06:56.516 --> 00:07:00.553
-Thank you, Ikea, for posting...

00:07:00.553 --> 00:07:02.121
-Waaah!
-...the recipe

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:04.290
for your Swedish meatballs
online.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:05.758
It's great, but I still
don't understand

00:07:05.758 --> 00:07:07.426
why I have
all these screws left over.

00:07:07.426 --> 00:07:08.894
-Waaah!

00:07:08.894 --> 00:07:10.496
-Can I have some music, please?

00:07:12.164 --> 00:07:13.299
♪♪

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:14.500
-Waaah!

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:15.801
-Thank you, Disney,

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:18.370
for announcing Season 3
of "The Mandalorian"

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:21.974
and giving us all a chance to
brace ourselves for Tween Yoda.

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:24.810
[ Laughter ]
-Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo!

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.045
-"Out of my room get."

00:07:26.045 --> 00:07:27.914
-Boo!
-[ Chuckles ]

00:07:27.914 --> 00:07:29.215
-Boo!

00:07:29.215 --> 00:07:30.883
-"Know -- Know me you don't."

00:07:30.883 --> 00:07:33.285
[ Laughs ]
-Boo!

00:07:33.285 --> 00:07:34.319
Boo!
-Um.

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:37.222
-[ Laughs ]
-Thank you,

00:07:37.222 --> 00:07:40.659
Popeyes' new blueberry and
lemon cream cheese pie,

00:07:40.659 --> 00:07:44.931
for sounding like a dessert
designed by a slot machine.

00:07:44.931 --> 00:07:48.167
Can I have some music, please?
-Boo!

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:49.669
Boo!
-[ Chuckles ]

00:07:49.669 --> 00:07:51.270
-Can I have some music, please?
Thank you.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:52.638
-You're welcome.
-Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo!

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:54.807
[ Laughter ]
-Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo!

00:07:54.807 --> 00:07:57.876
-Thank you morning, noon,
and night,

00:07:57.876 --> 00:07:59.879
for merging
and becoming one thing

00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:02.281
that I like to call
"mornnoonight."

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:04.283
[ Laughter ]
-Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo!

00:08:04.283 --> 00:08:06.953
[ Laughs ] You know,
it's almost bedtime, you guys.

00:08:06.953 --> 00:08:09.888
Ha ha ha ha!
-Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo!

00:08:09.888 --> 00:08:10.956
-Thank you...

00:08:10.956 --> 00:08:13.125
♪♪

00:08:13.125 --> 00:08:15.561
-Boo! Boo!

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:17.730
Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo!

00:08:18.997 --> 00:08:22.835
♪ Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo!
Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo! ♪

00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:24.103
♪♪

00:08:24.103 --> 00:08:26.939
♪ Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo!
Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo! ♪

00:08:26.939 --> 00:08:28.740
-♪ Boo! Boo! Boo! ♪

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:30.509
♪ Boo! Boo! Boo-boo! Boo! ♪
[ Laughter ]

00:08:30.509 --> 00:08:32.278
♪ Boo! Boo! Boo! ♪

00:08:32.278 --> 00:08:34.179
♪ Boo! Boo! Boo-boo! Boo! ♪

00:08:34.179 --> 00:08:35.815
♪ Boo! Boo! ♪

00:08:35.815 --> 00:08:38.684
♪ Boo! Boo! Boo-boo!
Boo! Boo! Boo-boo! ♪

00:08:38.684 --> 00:08:39.819
♪ Boo! Boo! Boo-boo! ♪

00:08:39.819 --> 00:08:41.020
All right, thank you, China,

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:43.221
for building the world's
largest sports stadium

00:08:43.221 --> 00:08:44.757
and for answering the question,

00:08:44.757 --> 00:08:46.759
what's the opposite
of good timing?

00:08:46.759 --> 00:08:47.826
-[ Chuckles ]

00:08:47.826 --> 00:08:48.860
-Can I have music, please?

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:51.464
-[ Vocalizing ]

00:08:54.933 --> 00:08:56.068
-And thank you, con--

00:08:56.068 --> 00:08:57.369
-[ Vocalizing ]

00:08:57.369 --> 00:08:59.438
-Thank you,
contactless food delivery,

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:02.008
for making me feel like a bear
that's being lured out of a cave

00:09:02.008 --> 00:09:04.343
by a piece of meat left outside.

00:09:05.878 --> 00:09:07.012
♪♪

00:09:07.012 --> 00:09:08.214
-Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo! Boo!

00:09:08.214 --> 00:09:09.582
-Thank you, homeschooling...

00:09:09.582 --> 00:09:11.083
[ Laughter ]

00:09:11.083 --> 00:09:13.819
♪♪

00:09:13.819 --> 00:09:15.922
Thank you, homeschooling,
for showing us

00:09:15.922 --> 00:09:18.324
that recess
is really for teachers.

00:09:18.324 --> 00:09:20.125
-[ Laughs ]
-♪ Boo! Boo! Boo-boo! ♪

00:09:20.125 --> 00:09:21.727
♪ Boo! Boo!
Boo! Boo! Boo-boo! ♪

00:09:21.727 --> 00:09:23.562
And, finally,
thank you sweatpants --

00:09:23.562 --> 00:09:26.198
or, as I now call you,
leg napkins.

00:09:26.198 --> 00:09:28.667
There you go.
That is our "thank you" notes.

00:09:28.667 --> 00:09:30.536
Thank you guys so much
for helping.

00:09:30.536 --> 00:09:31.803
That was so helpful.

00:09:31.803 --> 00:09:34.507
That is our "thank you" notes.
Thank you.

00:09:34.507 --> 00:09:36.942
[ Laughter ]

00:09:36.942 --> 00:09:39.211
We'll be right back, everybody,
with more "Tonight Show."

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:40.546
Come on back.

